## Answer to the user's goal question

**Frontend IS backend-switch-ready for the data layer**: every page
renders exclusively from the injected `ApiClient` (one source; page
fixtures are gone), every ApiClient method has a `docs/apis/*` contract,
and the switch is ONE flag: `environment.useMock: false` (+ apiUrl).
Remaining work is NOT data-source work — it's the planned packs:

- **B — state**: signal stores (auth/pool/opportunities/executions/
  payouts/communities/notifications) + one ThemeService (theme logic
  still copied in 5 files)
- **C — auth**: route guards (none exist), token refresh, 2FA UI, KYC
  flow (TokenStore + interceptor + login/register are wired)
- **D — flows**: deposit/withdraw/vote/submit-signal mutations still
  local state (pages render mock data but submit flows don't POST)
- **E — remaining**: landing template split (1109 lines), any leftover
  doc refresh

